05 GiB memory\n\n### Issue description\n\nIn the Scene Editor, all Controls are rendered with `display/window/size/viewport_width/height`, which makes them appear blurry when the initial viewport size is small or zoomed in. This is especially problematic when dealing with fonts, for example, in pixel art games where only fonts are rendered with retina quality, see these two screenshots of fonts in Scene Editor vs Runtime visuals:\n\n<img width=\"441\" height=\"345\" alt=\"Image\" src=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/ece597b0-ca74-4b70-85eb-2d70c89e5ffd\" />\n\n<img width=\"327\" height=\"272\" alt=\"Image\" src=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/a642f65a-1ebf-4587-9cc3-64173ec371b0\" />\n\n### Steps to reproduce\n\n1. Download the Mrp.\n2. Open it with the Godot Editor 4.5.1\n3. Inspect the Label Visuals in Editor.\n\n<img width=\"1945\" height=\"1117\" alt=\"image\" src=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/e275a614-86dc-4cd5-bc1a-10815b544ee4\" />\n\n4. Click Play, and Inspect the Label Visuals in Runtime.\n\n<img width=\"2568\" height=\"1704\" alt=\"image\" src=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/ebd0e273-3d34-40d9-8183-df2a8c6723d9\" />\n\n\n### Minimal reproduction project (MRP)\n\n[mrp_blur_label_2025-12-19_22-06-25.zip](https://github.com/user-attachments/files/24259358/mrp_blur_label_2025-12-19_22-06-25.zip)","closed_by":{"login":"Repiteo","id":17489292,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE3NDg5Mjky","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/17489292?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo","html_url":"https://github.com/Repiteo","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/subscriptions","organizations_u